;; A first run's later strata must see every row an earlier stratum wrote.
;; A first run creates each relation in its prepared boundary with only the
;; identity ordering, a placeholder until the program's own orderings
;; arrive.  The first stratum here (goal, seed, part: facts and a recursive
;; probe of goal by its second column) maintains goal in (1 0) alone; the
;; ones after it scan goal and probe it by its first column, through (0 1).
;; The placeholder must not pass for that maintained (0 1): it holds none of
;; goal's rows.
table (goal str int)
table (seed int)
table (part str int)
table (every str)
table (answer str int)

rule (goal "a" 1)
rule (goal "b" 2)
rule (goal "c" 1)
rule (seed 1)

rule (seed N) (goal G N) --> (part G N)
rule (part G N) --> (goal G N) (seed N)
rule (goal G N) --> (every G)
rule (every G) (goal G N) --> (answer G N)
